# Cursor Rules for Hugo Static Site Project

## Project Overview
This is a Hugo static site project using the Eureka theme, deployed to GitHub Pages.

## Technology Stack
- **Static Site Generator**: Hugo (v0.110.0+)
- **Theme**: Eureka (wangchucheng.com/hugo-eureka)
- **Deployment**: GitHub Pages via GitHub Actions
- **Content Format**: Markdown with frontmatter

## Project Structure
- `content/` - All content files (posts, docs, pages)
- `config/_default/` - Hugo configuration files
- `layouts/` - Custom templates and layouts
- `static/` - Static assets (images, JS, CSS)
- `assets/` - Source assets that may be processed
- `.github/workflows/` - GitHub Actions workflows

## Content Management
- Content files are in Markdown format with YAML frontmatter
- Posts go in `content/posts/`
- Documentation goes in `content/docs/`
- Pages go in `content/homepage/`
- Author information in `content/authors/`

## Code Style Guidelines
- Use consistent Markdown formatting
- Frontmatter should include: title, date, tags/categories when applicable
- Follow existing content structure patterns
- Use Chinese language for content (defaultContentLanguage: zh)

## Hugo Commands
- `hugo` - Build site locally
- `hugo server` - Start local development server
- `hugo --gc --minify` - Build for production with garbage collection and minification

## Git Workflow
- Main branch: `main`
- Auto-deployment: Pushes to main trigger GitHub Actions workflow
- Never commit `public/` directory (it's in .gitignore)

## Important Notes
- Base URL: https://zjingwang.github.io/
- The site uses Hugo Modules for theme management
- GitHub Actions automatically builds and deploys on push to main
- Local development: run `hugo server` and visit http://localhost:1313

